<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:31:22Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russian GRU spies behind failed Leipzig attack: reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5412c154609485fb576b786c8291c2cd8146f392197c7c3f2574f9b30f022eb7</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858--97143d694fa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German newspaper has cited reports tying a failed attack at Leipzig Airport to Moscow's GRU military intelligence agency. One suspect's ties to GRU were known when he entered the country, yet he was not surveilled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany charges 7 suspected Hamas members over attack plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a845b98e03a7e227b46d938fb21b6b1dda23e25d93d5d1ace3a87dc65d6c5be</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T11:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171--a30b5fe0228d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-charges-7-suspected-hamas-members-over-attack-plot/a-79230171?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prosecutors say the suspects had moved beyond general preparations and were already pursuing a concrete plan for a deadly attack on Israeli or Jewish targets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Thousands protest against AfD in Düsseldorf</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4772622ca95de400465a3f0f13a746a896cfeeb94d9385e46bac139a1f40bfaa</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:31:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-protest-against-afd-in-d_sseldorf/live-79223427--8b1953646143.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-thousands-protest-against-afd-in-düsseldorf/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police said around 20,000 people demonstrated in Düsseldorf under the slogan "Not a Step Back!" to protest the Alternative for Germany (AfD) party and right-wing hate speech. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Turks in Germany anxious after AfD wins in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8823d33e6ead0bfb5d2efca9d2265d581069f753497d0b24f7fe5f095473c315</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T10:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764--9bdd69d84853.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turks-in-germany-anxious-after-afd-wins-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79221764?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Alternative for Germany party's win in Saxony-Anhalt has alarmed people of Turkish origin in eastern states. Will workers and business owners abandon the increasingly AfD-friendly region for the more welcoming west?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's connection to the 9/11 attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff2544e775e5f4750f7697ddc74e9c7596a55ce94bcac64ec4100d693883201f</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T06:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918--33622f8e5007.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-connection-to-the-9-11-attacks/a-79202918?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 9/11 plot, including the twin tower attacks, was partly planned by the so-called Hamburg cell. A look at how Germany's national security was reshaped.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany sets its sights on Russia's shadow fleet</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7262a66ad3342c69f6ea64666b5c0d39b823bda6822f5b8e6ec8679b6f4f4a4</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T17:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123--786b113b7d97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-sets-its-sights-on-russia-s-shadow-fleet/a-79211123?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The German government wants to follow other EU countries and take more decisive action against Russia's shadow fleet, accusing it of helping Moscow evade sanctions and carry out acts of sabotage.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Herzog: Germany's wild man of cinema is back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9fdb2404e0224d54167320cc5adda56cdfad936ca6f8aa9bc66f64c0cee64c7</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324--4a5372e58812.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-herzog-germany-s-wild-man-of-cinema-is-back/a-78949324?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As his latest movie, "Bucking Fastard," premiered at the Venice Film Festival, DW talked to the boundary-breaking director.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc771cafe938</id><updated>2026-09-12T18:30:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T08:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997--9bbbc99c220c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-beethoven-festival-evokes-a-sense-of-home/a-78892997?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The motto of this year's classical music festival in Bonn is "Home/At Home," featuring musicians from diverse cultures presenting pieces from their homelands.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry></feed>
